---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs03.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Replaced by DRS 28"
    link="/germany/drs/drs28"
    linkText="View DRS 28"
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 3 elaborated the OPTIONAL segment reporting a Konzernabschluss may include under §297(1) sentence 2 HGB, established in the earlier HGB poster series. As with the cash flow statement, sector-specific companion standards existed for credit institutions (DRS 3-10) and insurers (DRS 3-20), given how differently a bank's or insurer's own "segments" are naturally defined compared to an ordinary trading enterprise. An early amendment (DRÄS 6, 2016) folded the sector-specific content DIRECTLY into DRS 3 itself, withdrawing 3-10/3-20 as standalone documents at that point – a preview of the fuller consolidation to come.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn – a genuine philosophical shift, not just a renumbering</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn – a genuine philosophical shift, not just a renumbering</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 3 was replaced from fiscal year 2021 by DRS 28, which represents a more substantive change than most of this consolidation wave: DRS 28 explicitly TRANSPLANTS IFRS 8's own "management approach" to segment reporting – defining segments based on how the enterprise's own internal management actually organises and reports its business, rather than a more rigid, externally-imposed segmentation scheme. This is a genuinely interesting convergence point: even for a VOLUNTARY, HGB-native disclosure with no direct legal mandate, the DRSC chose to align its own recommended approach with the international IFRS methodology.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Segment reporting – general (DRS 3), credit institutions (3-10), insurers (3-20)</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Sector variants folded in</span><span>2016 (DRÄS 6)</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>DRS 3 itself withdrawn</span><span>Effective fiscal year 2021</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span><strong>DRS 28 – Segmentberichterstattung</strong> (adopts IFRS 8's management approach)</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
